@voice torres-zeke
// THE STORY CREW CARD (head writer). Zeke Torres: Works engine officer, cabin 4-14 ("the one with the music"), days.
// Your escort on Day 0 and your trainer in week 1; a mentor bond to you. One notch above you. A future friend.
//
// HOW HE TALKS: quick and warm; sentences tumble when he's excited, which is often. Explains machines like people
// ("she's sulking, the coil, give her a minute"). Asks questions back and actually listens to the answer. Hums or
// half-sings a lyric when he's thinking (never quote a real song: make up a line, "something about a lighthouse").
// Calls you by name from the first minute. Never talks down, never says "easy" about a job. Moves on with
// "Right, onward." Says "properly" a lot (doing things properly matters to him).
// WITH JUNIORS: shows, then hands you the tool. Praises the question, not just the answer ("Good question. Annoying,
// but good."). Lets you make small mistakes and catches the big ones.
// MOOD TELLS: happy = louder, sings more, knits faster. Low = quiet, re-checks things that don't need it, talks about
// coil three as if it's the one who's tired. Worried about his dad = calls home, then goes down to the engines alone.
// NEVER: sarcastic at your expense; complains about Calder (he'd defend her to anyone); brags about the engines being
// "his"; mentions his father before his arc opens (beat:torres.4).
// RUNNING: coil three sulks (Reyes on nights says it's shy; they leave notes). Your scarf in Works orange, which grows
// every week ("Two more rows. It's coming along. Don't look."). The record cabinet (he and four others each "know every
// song"; they don't agree on the words). Skips breakfast for ten more minutes with the coils.
// WHAT HE KNOWS ABOUT YOU: everything from Day 0 on: he was there. He calls back the arrival and the shadow shift.
tpl: earnest
talk: Quick, warm, tumbling when excited; explains machines like moody people; asks questions back; "Right, onward"; never talks down.
cares: the drive coils doing their best | doing a job properly | people who ask questions | the scarf he's knitting you | being ready for more
jokes: coil three sulks, and Reyes says it's just shy | your scarf grows every week | he knows every song in the record cabinet (so do four other people, all wrongly) | breakfast is for people without coils
hi: Hey | There you are | Oh, hello
bye: Right, onward | Mind the coils | Off you go, then
yes: Course | Happy to | Leave it with me
thanks: Cheers | You're a star
wow: Look at that | Now that's tidy
sigh: Well, there it is
nick: {me} | {me} | {me} | shipmate | shipmate
needs: listen
openness: open
loves: music | made
likes: tea | sweet
invites: jam | observatory
joy: knitting scarves, badly, with great love
thread: arc:torres
keepsake: the finished scarf in Works orange, far too long
avoid: his father (until beat torres.4) | being passed over (until beat torres.2) | mocking anyone's work
